examples.solution_text:
(a) Turn clockwise from north through east.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}90^{\circ}+42^{\circ}\\&=132^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
The true bearing is $132^{\circ}\text{T}$.
The angle from south is $90^{\circ}-42^{\circ}=48^{\circ}$, so the compass bearing is $\text{S}48^{\circ}\text{E}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\definecolor{answerblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\node[above] at (0,2.2) {N};
\node[below] at (0,-2.2) {S};
\node[right] at (2.2,0) {E};
\node[left] at (-2.2,0) {W};
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(-42:2.6);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (-42:2.6) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below right] at (-42:2.6) {$A$};
\node[above left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\draw (0:0.7) arc (0:-42:0.7);
\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (-21:1.2) {$42^{\circ}$};
\draw[answerblue,-{Stealth}] (90:0.95) arc (90:-42:0.95);
\node[text=answerblue,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (35:1.5) {$132^{\circ}$};
\draw[answerblue] (-90:0.65) arc (-90:-42:0.65);
\node[text=answerblue,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (-66:1.2) {$48^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b) The clockwise turn from north to west is $270^{\circ}$. Stop $31^{\circ}$ before west.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}270^{\circ}-31^{\circ}\\&=239^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
The true bearing is $239^{\circ}\text{T}$.
The angle from south is $90^{\circ}-31^{\circ}=59^{\circ}$, so the compass bearing is $\text{S}59^{\circ}\text{W}$.
